tags: instance-name

A setting of a start, from the caller: the name that the caller gives to the instance.
The node shows it to its operator and to the caller. It is not an id: two instances can
have the same name.

The value is lowercase ASCII letters and digits in groups separated by one "-", 1 to 63
characters. Example: brisk-falcon.

With no setting, the node selects a name. The node is bound: it refuses a value that
does not have this form.

=== formal
class=setting
default=absent: the node selects a name
name=instance-name
place=configuration
value=[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*, 1 to 63 characters
